o place."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5329,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5329},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2460db03-fc58-42a8-aad5-8896829fe062","uuid":"a906bcf3-0185-4dcb-87b6-f606d60d2e53","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:24:14.011Z","request_id":"req_011CgjYC6PsHHZMLfvJy9dg7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SaQ84XQr3Zb9hhMSgQf7iJ":{"working":"Start: a scrawl at the left edge, then a clef with two flats about 300 px in. A clef and key signature in mid-line usually means a new section starts here. After them comes a large note with a flourish and a half-note-like shape, then a barline. Next bars:\n- rest + short note (a quarter-note figure)\n- a 'p'-like mark over a rest and short notes\n- two quarter notes near the middle line (about D3)\n- 'for' over a rest and two notes\n- a nearly empty bar or two of rests\n- 'for' over a rest and a note\n- a bar of four quarter-like notes\n- a bar of about three or four quarter notes\n\nThe line ends on a dotted half and a double bar with repeat dots.\n\nEdition bars 55–60 are steady repeated 8ths, six per bar (Bb2, Bb2, A2, Bb2, D3, Eb3), then F3 8ths, a dotted-half Bb2 (61), and the Eb2–F2 8th figure (62). A copyist might abbreviate repeated 8ths, but this line has no such run. Its bars are full of rests and two-note figures marked 'for', with no strokes for repeated notes. The notes sit near D3, not on Bb2. There is a dotted half, but it comes at the very end, before a double bar. The edition has no double bar anywhere in bars 52–65, and bar 61's dotted half is followed by 8ths. The rests, the 'for' marks, the mid-line clef and the closing repeat do not f